{"text":"The citizens of Nicomedia spent three million three hundred and twenty-nine sesterces on an aqueduct that was not finished, and a second attempt also failed.","citations": [{"id": "pliny:XLVI:1", "path": "vault/raw/pliny.html#link2H_4_0157", "quote": "THE citizens of Nicomedia, Sir, have expended three millions three hundred and twenty-nine sesterces in building an aqueduct; but, not being able to finish it, the works are entirely falling to ruin."}]}
],
    "text":"Pliny suggested using remaining square stones from the first building to turn the new arches, and that brick might be a cheaper and easier material for raising parts of the work.","citations": [{"id": "pliny:XLVI:1", "path": "vault/raw/pliny.html#link2H_4_0157", "quote": "There are still remaining a very few of the old arches; and the square stones, however, employed in the former building, may be used in turning the new arches. I am of opinion part should be raised with brick, as that will be the easier and cheaper material."}]}
